Backport of lxc/incus@7c998495cf7f3f8f658492a116c7e15288ac9993 (stable-7.0; on main as
e00b75d4a) to v7.0.2 for the isx appliance (Sanne/incus-spawn#2104), unchanged: part of the fix for
GHSA-3wxw-5gh2-j2x2: loader variables such as LD_PRELOAD from an instance or image environment no
longer reach the root forklxc process and its hooks.
Remove this file once INCUS_VERSION is a release that contains the commit (the next 7.0
release; 7.0.3 is not out yet).

From 7c998495cf7f3f8f658492a116c7e15288ac9993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Graber?= <stgraber@stgraber.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:28:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] incusd/instance/lxc: Keep loader variables out of the forklxc
 environment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Instance and image environment variables are passed to the root forklxc
process so application containers inherit them. Variables such as
LD_PRELOAD would also apply to forklxc and to the hooks it runs, so skip
those. They still reach the container through lxc.environment.

This addresses GHSA-3wxw-5gh2-j2x2 (CVE pending)

Signed-off-by: Stéphane Graber <stgraber@stgraber.org>
---
 internal/server/instance/drivers/driver_lxc.go | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/internal/server/instance/drivers/driver_lxc.go b/internal/server/instance/drivers/driver_lxc.go
index c62d4c8b5..eb868dfdd 100644
--- a/internal/server/instance/drivers/driver_lxc.go
+++ b/internal/server/instance/drivers/driver_lxc.go
@@ -178,6 +178,12 @@ func lxcSetConfigItem(c *liblxc.Container, key string, value string) error {
 	return nil
 }
 
+// forklxcBlockedEnv returns whether an instance or image environment variable must be kept out of
+// the root forklxc process, as it would alter the behavior of the dynamic loader or of glibc.
+func forklxcBlockedEnv(name string) bool {
+	return strings.HasPrefix(name, "LD_") || slices.Contains([]string{"GCONV_PATH", "GLIBC_TUNABLES"}, name)
+}
+
 // isOCI returns whether the container was created from an OCI image.
 func (d *lxc) isOCI() bool {
 	return util.IsTrue(d.expandedConfig["volatile.container.oci"]) || d.localConfig["image.type"] == "oci"
@@ -3214,7 +3220,7 @@ func (d *lxc) start(stateful bool, op *operationlock.InstanceOperation) error {
 
 	for k, v := range d.expandedConfig {
 		after, ok := strings.CutPrefix(k, "environment.")
-		if ok {
+		if ok && !forklxcBlockedEnv(after) {
 			envDict[after] = v
 		}
 	}
@@ -3235,7 +3241,7 @@ func (d *lxc) start(stateful bool, op *operationlock.InstanceOperation) error {
 
 		for k, v := range ociEnv {
 			_, ok := envDict[k]
-			if !ok {
+			if !ok && !forklxcBlockedEnv(k) {
 				envDict[k] = v
 			}
 		}
-- 
